CMonTensor -- the signature tensor of the canonical monomial path at a given level
**********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        s = CAxisTensor(k, R)
  * Inputs:
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the level of the signature
        tensor to compute;
      * R, an instance of the type *note NCPolynomialRing:
        (NCAlgebra)NCPolynomialRing,, the output tensor space;
  * Outputs:
      * s, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,, an element of R; the k-th level signature of
        the canonical monomial path in $\mathbb R^d$, where $d$ is the number
        of generators of R;

Description
===========

The canonical monomial path in $\mathbb{R}^d$ is the path from $(0, \dots, 0)$
to $(1, \dots, 1)$ given by $t\mapsto (t, t^2, \dots, t^d)$. Its $k$-th level
signature has a closed-form description (see the reference below) and can be
obtained as follows:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : d = 2;                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : k = 3;                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = wordAlgebra(d);                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Cd = CMonTensor(k, R); Cd // wordFormat --k-th level signature of the ca|
|                                                                             |
|     1              1              2              1              4           |
|o5 = - [2, 2, 2] + -- [2, 2, 1] + -- [2, 1, 2] + -- [2, 1, 1] + -- [1, 2, 2] |
|     6             10             15             12             15           |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|       1             1             1                                         |
|     + - [1, 2, 1] + - [1, 1, 2] + - [1, 1, 1]                               |
|       6             4             6                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|nonical monomial path in R^d                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

To expand on the example, we verify that the result agrees with the one
obtained from *note sig: sig,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R=QQ[t];                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : CMonPath = polyPath(for i from 1 to d list t^i) -- The canonical axis   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = Path in 2-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:                  |
|                                                                             |
|           2                                                                 |
|     {{t, t }}                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Path                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|path in dimension d                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : Cd2 = sig(CMonPath, k); Cd2 // wordFormat --The k-th level signature    |
|                                                                             |
|     1              1              2              1              4           |
|o9 = - [2, 2, 2] + -- [2, 2, 1] + -- [2, 1, 2] + -- [2, 1, 1] + -- [1, 2, 2] |
|     6             10             15             12             15           |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|       1             1             1                                         |
|     + - [1, 2, 1] + - [1, 1, 2] + - [1, 1, 1]                               |
|       6             4             6                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

