halfshuffle -- compute the half-shuffle of an ordered pair of words
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        h = f >> g
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,,
      * g, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,,
  * Outputs:
      * h, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,, the half-shuffle f>>g of the two words;

Description
===========

We start with the mathematical definition, based on [1] (see #ref1 ) (where the
operation is called right half-shuffle). Let $T^{\geq 1}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be the
vector space spanned by the non empty words on $d$ letters. Then the half
shuffle $>>$ is defined recursively to be $$ w >> i := wi$$ for $w$ a word and
$i$ a letter and $$ w >> vi := (w >> v + v >> w)\bullet i$$ for $w, v$ words
and $i$ a letter, where $\bullet$ is the concatenation product on words.

As stated in the reference, the *note shuffle: (Macaulay2Doc)shuffle, on non
empty words can be seen as a symmetrization of the half-shuffle. As a usage
example, we verify this in a particular instance.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = wordAlgebra(3);                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : w = [1]_R                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Lt                                                                      |
|       1                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : v = [1,2,3]_R                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Lt Lt Lt                                                                |
|       1  2  3                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : s = w ** v --shuffle product of w, v                                    |
|                                                                             |
|                                   2                                         |
|o4 = Lt Lt Lt Lt +Lt Lt Lt Lt +2Lt  Lt Lt                                    |
|       1  2  3  1   1  2  1  3    1   2  3                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : hsSymm = (w >> v) + (v >> w)--half-shuffle product symmetrization of w, |
|                                                                             |
|                                   2                                         |
|o5 = Lt Lt Lt Lt +Lt Lt Lt Lt +2Lt  Lt Lt                                    |
|       1  2  3  1   1  2  1  3    1   2  3                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : R                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|v                                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : s == hsSymm                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

References
==========

[1] Signatures of paths transformed by polynomial maps
(doi.org/10.1007/s13366-020-00493-9) (see
https://doi.org/10.1007/s13366-020-00493-9 )

See also
========

  * *note shuffle: (Macaulay2Doc)shuffle, -- shuffle a list randomly
  * Array _ NCPolynomialRing (missing documentation)

Ways to use halfshuffle:
========================

  * "halfshuffle(NCRingElement,NCRingElement)"

