lie -- lie bracket of two elements
**********************************

  * Usage: 
        c = lie(a, b)
  * Inputs:
      * a, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,,
      * b, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,,
  * Outputs:
      * c, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,, The commutator of a, b;

Description
===========

A non-commutative algebra $(R, +, \cdot)$ is naturally a Lie algebra with the
commutator $a\cdot b - b\cdot a$ as the Lie bracket. The commutator of two
non-commutative polynomials can be computed as follows:

+-------------------------+
|i1 : R = wordAlgebra (3);|
+-------------------------+
|i2 : a = [1]_R           |
|                         |
|o2 = Lt                  |
|       1                 |
|                         |
|o2 : R                   |
+-------------------------+
|i3 : b = [2]_R           |
|                         |
|o3 = Lt                  |
|       2                 |
|                         |
|o3 : R                   |
+-------------------------+
|i4 : lie(a,b)            |
|                         |
|o4 = -Lt Lt +Lt Lt       |
|        2  1   1  2      |
|                         |
|o4 : R                   |
+-------------------------+

