lyndonWords -- compute all Lyndon words of at most a given length on a given number of letters
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = lyndonWords(d, k)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The number of letters; 
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The maximum length; 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of all Lyndon words of length at
        most k in d letters;

Description
===========

A word $l$ on the alphabet $\{1,\dots, d\}$ is a Lyndon word if it is strictly
smaller, in lexicographic order, than all of its rotations.

This method generates a list containing all Lyndon words of length at most $k$
on $d$ letters. The Lyndon words are given as *note Array: (Macaulay2Doc)Array,
in the same convention of *note wordFormat: wordFormat,.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : words = lyndonWords (2,3)               |
|                                             |
|o1 = {[1], [1, 1, 2], [1, 2], [1, 2, 2], [2]}|
|                                             |
|o1 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = wordAlgebra(2);                     |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : apply(words, i-> i_R)                   |
|                                             |
|              2                   2          |
|o3 = {Lt , Lt  Lt , Lt Lt , Lt Lt  , Lt }    |
|        1    1   2    1  2    1  2     2     |
|                                             |
|o3 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

