File: PathSignatures.info, Node: Path, Next: polyPath, Prev: NCRingElement, Up: Top

Path
****

Description
===========

A polynomial path is a map $[0,1] \to \mathbb R^d$ whose coordinate functions
are given by polynomials. A piecewise polynomial path is a concatenation of
polynomial paths.

To create a polynomial path, use *note polyPath: polyPath,, which takes a list
of polynomials as input. These can be given as elements of a commutative
polynomial ring with one generator or directly in *note listForm:
(Macaulay2Doc)listForm,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[t];                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = polyPath({t,2*t^2,3*t^3})                         |
|                                                           |
|o2 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:|
|                                                           |
|            2    3                                         |
|     {{t, 2t , 3t }}                                       |
|                                                           |
|o2 : Path                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Y = polyPath({{({1},1)},{({2},2)},{({3},3)}})         |
|                                                           |
|o3 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:|
|                                                           |
|            2    3                                         |
|     {{t, 2t , 3t }}                                       |
|                                                           |
|o3 : Path                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

While the polynomials must be chosen from a polynomial ring with one generator,
the coefficient ring of the polynomials can be chosen arbitrarily.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[a][t]; --QQ[a,t] will not work!                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : X = polyPath({t,2*a*t^2,3*a^2*t^3})                   |
|                                                           |
|o5 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:|
|                                                           |
|              2    2 3                                     |
|     {{t, 2a*t , 3a t }}                                   |
|                                                           |
|o5 : Path                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

An important special case of polynomial paths are linear paths. These can be
constructed directly from their increment using *note linPath: linPath,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Y = linPath({2,3,4})                                  |
|                                                           |
|o6 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:|
|                                                           |
|     {{2t, 3t, 4t}}                                        |
|                                                           |
|o6 : Path                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

Paths can be concatenated using *note Path ** Path: concatPath,. This
concatenation is formal: the new Path object encodes the polynomial pieces and
their order, but no parametrization is chosen. The concatenation *note Path **
Path: concatPath, will automatically select a bigger coefficient ring for all
polynomial pieces if an obvious choice is available.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Z = X ** Y                                             |
|                                                            |
|o7 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 2 polynomial segments:|
|                                                            |
|              2    2 3                                      |
|     {{t, 2a*t , 3a t }, {2t, 3t, 4t}}                      |
|                                                            |
|o7 : Path                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

A piecewise linear path can be constructed directly from the increments of its
segments using *note pwLinPath: pwLinPath,.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A = matrix {{1,2,3},{2,3,4},{4,5,6}};                  |
|                                                            |
|              3       3                                     |
|o8 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : W = pwLinPath(A)                                       |
|                                                            |
|o9 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 3 polynomial segments:|
|                                                            |
|     {{t, 2t, 4t}, {2t, 3t, 5t}, {3t, 4t, 6t}}              |
|                                                            |
|o9 : Path                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

To read out the ambient dimension of a path, use *note getDimension(Path):
Path, or *note dim(Path): Path,. To get the pieces of the path in *note
listForm: (Macaulay2Doc)listForm, use *note getPieces(Path): Path,. To get the
coefficient ring of the coordinate polynomials, use *note
getCoefficientRing(Path): Path, or *note coefficientRing(Path): Path,. Finally,
*note getNumberOfPieces(Path): Path, returns the number of pieces of the path.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : getDimension(Z) --The ambient dimension of the path                    |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = 3                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : getPieces(Z) --The polynomial pieces of the path, in listForm          |
|                                                                             |
|                                          2                                  |
|o11 = {{{({1}, 1)}, {({2}, 2a)}, {({3}, 3a )}}, {{({1}, 2)}, {({1}, 3)},     |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      {({1}, 4)}}}                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : getCoefficientRing(Z) -- The coefficient ring of the polynomial        |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = QQ[a]                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o12 : PolynomialRing                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|components of the path                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : getNumberOfPieces(Z) -- The number of polynomial pieces of the path    |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = 2                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

To extract the pieces of a concatenated path one can use *note Path _ ZZ:
Path,, *note Path _ List: Path, and *note Path _ Sequence: Path,.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : Z_0                                                               |
|                                                                        |
|o14 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:            |
|                                                                        |
|               2    2 3                                                 |
|      {{t, 2a*t , 3a t }}                                               |
|                                                                        |
|o14 : Path                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : Z2 = Z^2                                                          |
|                                                                        |
|o15 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 4 polynomial segments:           |
|                                                                        |
|               2    2 3                         2    2 3                |
|      {{t, 2a*t , 3a t }, {2t, 3t, 4t}, {t, 2a*t , 3a t }, {2t, 3t, 4t}}|
|                                                                        |
|o15 : Path                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : Z2_{0,-1}                                                         |
|                                                                        |
|o16 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 2 polynomial segments:           |
|                                                                        |
|               2    2 3                                                 |
|      {{t, 2a*t , 3a t }, {2t, 3t, 4t}}                                 |
|                                                                        |
|o16 : Path                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

When considering the set of paths modulo tree-like equivalence, concatenation
turns it into a groupoid. Use *note Path ^ ZZ: Path, to compute powers and the
inverse of a path in this groupoid. Note that the inverse of a path is just
given by reversing its parametrization.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : X^4                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o17 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 4 polynomial segments:                |
|                                                                             |
|               2    2 3           2    2 3           2    2 3           2    |
|      {{t, 2a*t , 3a t }, {t, 2a*t , 3a t }, {t, 2a*t , 3a t }, {t, 2a*t ,   |
|                                                                             |
|o17 : Path                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|  2 3                                                                        |
|3a t }}                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : X^(-1)                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o18 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:                 |
|                                                                             |
|                2             2 3     2 2     2                              |
|      {{-t, 2a*t  - 4a*t, - 3a t  + 9a t  - 9a t}}                           |
|                                                                             |
|o18 : Path                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note polyPath: polyPath, -- constructor of single piece polynomial path
  * *note linPath: linPath, -- constructor of single piece polynomial path

Functions and methods returning an object of class Path:
========================================================

  * "concatPath(Path,Path)" -- see *note concatPath: concatPath, --
    concatenation of paths
  * "Path ** Path" -- see *note concatPath: concatPath, -- concatenation of
    paths
  * "linPath(List)" -- see *note linPath: linPath, -- constructor of single
    piece polynomial path
  * "Path ^ ZZ"
  * "Path _ List"
  * "Path _ Sequence"
  * "Path _ ZZ"
  * "polyPath(List)" -- see *note polyPath: polyPath, -- constructor of single
    piece polynomial path
  * "pwLinPath(Matrix)" -- see *note pwLinPath: pwLinPath, -- constructor of a
    piecewise linear path from a matrix
  * *note substitute(Path,Ring): substitute_lpPath_cmRing_rp, -- changes the
    coefficient ring of a path

Methods that use an object of class Path:
=========================================

  * "coefficientRing(Path)"
  * "dim(Path)"
  * "getCoefficientRing(Path)"
  * "getDimension(Path)"
  * "getNumberOfPieces(Path)"
  * "getPieces(Path)"
  * "net(Path)"
  * "sig(Path,List)" -- see *note sig: sig, -- compute the signature of a
    piecewise polynomial path.
  * "sig(Path,NCRingElement)" -- see *note sig: sig, -- compute the signature
    of a piecewise polynomial path.
  * "sig(Path,ZZ)" -- see *note sig: sig, -- compute the signature of a
    piecewise polynomial path.
  * "sig(Path,ZZ,NCRing)" -- see *note sig: sig, -- compute the signature of a
    piecewise polynomial path.

