pwLinPath -- constructor of a piecewise linear path from a matrix
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        pwLinPath(pwlMatrix)
  * Inputs:
      * pwlMatrix, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, A matrix containing
        on its columns the articulation points (or increments) of the path;
  * Outputs:
      * X, an instance of the type *note Path: Path,, A piecewise linear path
        of dimension the number of rows of the input and with the same number
        of pieces as the columns of the input;

Description
===========

Creates a piecewise linear *note Path: Path, whose increments are the columns
of the given matrix.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = id_(QQ^3)                                          |
|                                                            |
|o1 = | 1 0 0 |                                              |
|     | 0 1 0 |                                              |
|     | 0 0 1 |                                              |
|                                                            |
|              3       3                                     |
|o1 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : pwLinPath(M)                                           |
|                                                            |
|o2 = Path in 3-dimensional space with 3 polynomial segments:|
|                                                            |
|     {{t, 0, 0}, {0, t, 0}, {0, 0, t}}                      |
|                                                            |
|o2 : Path                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

