shuffle(NCRingElement,NCRingElement) -- shuffle product of two words
********************************************************************

  * Function: *note shuffle: (Macaulay2Doc)shuffle,
  * Usage: 
        v = shuffle(w1, w2)
  * Inputs:
      * w1, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,,
      * w2, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,,
  * Outputs:
      * v, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,, The shuffle product of w1 and w2;

Description
===========

We start with the mathematical definition of this operation, based on [1] (see
#ref1 ). Consider $T(\mathbb{R}^d)$, the free algebra on the symbols $1,\dots,
d$. Denote by $\bullet$ its concatenation product and by $e$ the neutral
element with respect to the concatenation (the empty word). The shuffle product
of two words is defined recursively as follows. Let $w, w_1, w_2$ be three
words and $a, b$ bet two letters, i.e. $w, w_1, w_2\in T(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and
$a,b\in \{1,\dots, d\}$. Then the shuffle product $\char"29E2$ is defined to be
$$ e \char"29E2 w := w =: w\char"29E2 e$$ and $$(w_1\bullet a) \char"29E2
(w_2\bullet b) = (w_1 \char"29E2 (w_2\bullet b))\bullet a + ((w_1\bullet
a)\char"29E2 w_2)\bullet b$$

The easiest way to compute a shuffle product is through *note NCRingElement **
NCRingElement: shuffle_lpNCRingElement_cmNCRingElement_rp, which is equivalent
to *note shuffle(NCRingElement,NCRingElement):
shuffle_lpNCRingElement_cmNCRingElement_rp,:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = wordAlgebra(2); -- create a free associative algebra over two       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|letters Lt_1, Lt_2                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = [1,2]_R; -- [i_1,...,i_k]_R defines a word                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : wordFormat f -- display the polynomial in word notation                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = [1, 2]                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = ([1,2]_R ** [1,2]_R); -- compute the shuffle product                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f // wordFormat --display the result in word notation                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 2 [1, 2, 1, 2] + 4 [1, 1, 2, 2]                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

References
==========

[1] Signatures of paths transformed by polynomial maps
(doi.org/10.1007/s13366-020-00493-9) (see
https://doi.org/10.1007/s13366-020-00493-9 )

See also
========

  * *note wordAlgebra: wordAlgebra, -- create a free algebra over a given
    alphabet
