substitute(Path,Ring) -- changes the coefficient ring of a path
***************************************************************

  * Function: *note substitute: (Macaulay2Doc)substitute,
  * Usage: 
        Y = substitute(X,R)
  * Inputs:
      * X, an instance of the type *note Path: Path,, 
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, an algebra over the coefficient
        ring of the polynomials defining X;
  * Outputs:
      * Y, an instance of the type *note Path: Path,, a path with the same
        pieces as X but whose coordinate functions are now polynomials with
        coefficients in R;

Description
===========

Tries to substitute the coefficients of the polynomials defining the given path
into the given ring, producing a new path.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[t];                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = polyPath({t,t^2})                                 |
|                                                           |
|o2 = Path in 2-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:|
|                                                           |
|           2                                               |
|     {{t, t }}                                             |
|                                                           |
|o2 : Path                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : coefficientRing X                                     |
|                                                           |
|o3 = QQ                                                    |
|                                                           |
|o3 : Ring                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : A = QQ[a];                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Y = substitute(X,A)                                   |
|                                                           |
|o5 = Path in 2-dimensional space with 1 polynomial segment:|
|                                                           |
|           2                                               |
|     {{t, t }}                                             |
|                                                           |
|o5 : Path                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : coefficientRing Y                                     |
|                                                           |
|o6 = A                                                     |
|                                                           |
|o6 : PolynomialRing                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

