tensorArray -- k-th level component of a tensor.
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        sk = tensorArray(s,k)
        sk = s@k
        L = tensorArray(s)
  * Inputs:
      * s, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement:
        (NCAlgebra)NCRingElement,,
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The level to extract; 
  * Outputs:
      * sk, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, The k-th level of s, as a
        multi-dimensional array;
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, The list of all levels of s, as
        multi-dimensional arrays;

Description
===========

Returns the $k$-level component of a tensor as multi-dimensional array,
represented by a nested *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[t];                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = polyPath({t,t^2});                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : sig(X,2)@2 -- signature matrix at depth 2                               |
|                                                                             |
|       1  2    1  1                                                          |
|o3 = {{-, -}, {-, -}}                                                        |
|       2  3    3  2                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : A = sig(X,3)@3 -- third level signature as multi-dimensional array      |
|                                                                             |
|        1  1    1   4       1   2     1  1                                   |
|o4 = {{{-, -}, {-, --}}, {{--, --}, {--, -}}}                                |
|        6  4    6  15      12  15    10  6                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : i = 0; j = 0; k = 0;                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A#i#j#k == (Lt_(i+1)*Lt_(j+1)*Lt_(k+1))@(sig(X, 3)) --The coefficient of|
|                                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|(Lt_1)^3 in sig(X, 3)                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If the integer $k$ is not provided, returns a list of all non trivial levels
(in nested list form).

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : L = tensorArray(sig(X, 3))                                          |
|                                                                         |
|                                   1  1    1   4       1   2     1  1    |
|o9 = {{0, 0}, {{0, 0}, {0, 0}}, {{{-, -}, {-, --}}, {{--, --}, {--, -}}}}|
|                                   6  4    6  15      12  15    10  6    |
|                                                                         |
|o9 : List                                                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : L#2 == A                                                           |
|                                                                         |
|o10 = true                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

