tensorLog -- Compute a component of the logarithm of a tensor.
**************************************************************

Description
===========

Let $T((\mathbb{R}^d))$ denote the dual of the tensor algebra on
$\mathbb{R}^d$, i.e., the space $\prod_k (\mathbb{R}^d)^{\otimes k}$. Given $x
\in T(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with constant term $1$, its logarithm is $$\log(x) := -
\sum_{k \geq 0} \frac{1}{k} (1-x)^{\otimes k} \in T((\mathbb{R}^d)). $$
$\texttt{tensorLog(x,k)}$ computes the degree $k$ component of $\log(x)$.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A2 = wordAlgebra(2);                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x = 1 + [1]_A2 + 1/2 * [1,1]_A2 + 1/6 * [1,1,1]_A2;|
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : sum(0..3, i -> tensorLog(x, i))                    |
|                                                        |
|o3 = Lt                                                 |
|       1                                                |
|                                                        |
|o3 : A2                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The method is implemented only for tensors with constant term $1$.

See also
========

  * *note tensorExp: tensorExp, -- Compute a component of the exponential of a
    tensor.

Ways to use tensorLog:
======================

  * "tensorLog(NCRingElement,ZZ)"

